WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.760
Let's start with the foundation of your inner blueprint, your core values.

00:07.760 --> 00:12.320
Think of your values as your personal true North Star.

00:12.320 --> 00:18.440
But what happens when the true North Star is put to the test?

00:18.440 --> 00:24.160
There was a time I looked really good on paper, like I was winning.

00:24.160 --> 00:28.080
But honestly, I was running on fumes.

00:28.080 --> 00:35.640
I was pushing towards my goals to grow my family and my business, driven by my value

00:35.640 --> 00:37.280
of faith.

00:37.280 --> 00:45.520
But my body was fighting an undeniable disease, and I had to make a hard decision.

00:45.520 --> 00:48.840
That moment taught me a critical lesson.

00:48.840 --> 00:50.840
That wasn't failure.

00:50.840 --> 00:52.960
That was feedback.

00:52.960 --> 00:59.360
And the real breakthrough wasn't in pushing through, but in choosing to have surgery

00:59.360 --> 01:01.040
and recover.

01:01.040 --> 01:08.400
It was in that journey of transformation that I truly understood that rest isn't weakness.

01:08.400 --> 01:10.360
It's required.

01:10.360 --> 01:17.600
That's when values like wellbeing and resilience became powerful muscles that can redirect

01:17.600 --> 01:22.240
your North Star and redefine what truly success looks like.

01:22.720 --> 01:24.400
What it means to win.

01:24.400 --> 01:29.040
In fact, it's how the Athleadership movement was born.

01:29.040 --> 01:34.960
When your daily actions are aligned with your deepest values, you experience a sense of

01:34.960 --> 01:37.840
fulfillment and integrity.

01:37.840 --> 01:40.000
It just feels right.

01:40.000 --> 01:45.360
But when there's a disconnect, when you're asked to do something at work or in life that

01:45.360 --> 01:49.240
clashes with your core values, you feel it.

01:49.240 --> 01:54.760
It's that sense of friction, of burnout, and of being out of sync.

01:54.760 --> 01:58.680
An Athleader knows that this alignment is not a luxury.

01:58.680 --> 02:01.600
It's a competitive advantage.

02:01.600 --> 02:06.640
It allows you to make hard decisions faster and with more confidence.

02:12.240 --> 02:18.760
For example, if your family is a core value, it gives you the clarity to turn down a promotion

02:18.760 --> 02:21.120
requiring constant travel.

02:21.120 --> 02:27.200
If innovation is your core value, it gives you the courage to challenge the status quo,

02:27.200 --> 02:30.080
even when it's uncomfortable.

02:30.080 --> 02:35.320
In your playbook, we're going to guide you through a drill to move beyond a long list

02:35.320 --> 02:42.400
of nice sounding words to get crystal clear on the three to five values that truly define

02:42.400 --> 02:43.400
you.

02:43.400 --> 02:47.880
The reason we focus on just a few is that it forces clarity.

02:47.960 --> 02:52.000
Having 20 values is the same as having none.

02:52.000 --> 02:57.920
But knowing your three to five, that's a powerful decision making filter.

02:57.920 --> 03:02.200
Remember, this isn't about what you think your values should be.

03:02.200 --> 03:06.880
It's about uncovering what they already are.

03:06.880 --> 03:09.120
Take your time with this.

03:09.120 --> 03:13.280
This clarity will become the bedrock of your M.V.P. blueprint.

